From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: davmels <davmelous@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] ray.sub: PYXIS_EXTRA_ARGS for extra pyxis container flags

The pyxis path builds its srun flags from CONTAINER and MOUNTS only. Running
the EDF-described stacks under pyxis (KISTI HANGANG has no container engine)
also needs --container-writable and --container-env=<vars> so the exported
environment replaces the image's own values; PYXIS_EXTRA_ARGS carries them
instead of being smuggled through CONTAINER's word splitting.

---
 ray.sub | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ray.sub b/ray.sub
--- a/ray.sub
+++ b/ray.sub
@@ -232,6 +232,10 @@ else
   COMMON_SRUN_ARGS+=" --container-mounts=$MOUNTS"
   COMMON_SRUN_ARGS+=" --container-image=$CONTAINER"
   COMMON_SRUN_ARGS+=" --container-workdir=$SLURM_SUBMIT_DIR"
+  # Extra pyxis flags, e.g. --container-writable --container-env=VAR,... (word-split on purpose).
+  if [[ -n "${PYXIS_EXTRA_ARGS:-}" ]]; then
+    COMMON_SRUN_ARGS+=" $PYXIS_EXTRA_ARGS"
+  fi
   HEAD_CONTAINER_ARGS="--container-name=ray-head"
   WORKER_CONTAINER_ARGS="--container-name=ray-worker"
 fi
--
